					<p class="body1" align="left"><span class="body1 style73"> <h2>News archive</h2><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2006-11-13 | Monday</font></strong><br><br>Bittersweet November arrives chilly and wet in usual fashion. Big <font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" color="#333300"> up to the homie <strong>Amp Fire</strong> for pulling the 206 hip-hop scene together for a photo shoot of solidarity at the MLK memorial on Saturday. We&#39;ll post pictures as soon as we get &#39;em. Much love to everyone who performed and packed the Chop last Friday to witness the goodness that was <strong>Gabriel Teodros</strong>, <strong>Silent Lambs Project</strong>, <strong>D Black</strong> and <strong>Common Market</strong>, with <strong>DJ daps1</strong>. The night before at EMP, <strong>Geo</strong> held it down with a live band at <strong>UW &amp; SU&#39;s FASA JAM 2006</strong>, orchestrated by musician extraordinaire <strong>Orlando Morales</strong> (remember that name). In case you missed it, here&#39;s a clip of &quot;Life &amp; Debt&quot;:<br /><br /><object width="425" height="350" type="application/x-shockwave-flash" data="http://www.youtube.com/v/pzdO1JodLnM"><param name="movie" value="http://www.youtube.com/v/pzdO1JodLnM"></param><param name="wmode" value="transparent"></param></object></font><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2006-11-07 | Tuesday</font></strong><br><br><img src="../IMAGES/thaswassup.jpg" border="1" alt="" width="300" height="442" />  <p>Go pick up a copy of this month&#39;s <strong>URB Magazine</strong> (Perry Farrell/Immortal Technique cover) and peep <strong>Common Market&#39;s</strong> feature and 4.5 star review! <br /><br />Geo makes beats now. He also draws filthy, filthy pictures. Thanks to the sharp minds of your boys that are <strong>Abyssinian Creole</strong>, the &quot;new shit&quot; is to replace all statements of &quot;Thas Wassup&quot; with &quot;Filipino Warrior&quot; as inspired by the Geologic drawing that&#39;s been hanging in the office for a little over a week now.</p><p>To clarify, a phone conversation that went like this:</p><p>&quot;hello?&quot;<br />&quot;watt&#39;s good fam. where you at now?&quot;<br />&quot;coolin out with the kasamas at daps&#39; crib. we&#39;re checkin out his comic collection before we watch LOST.&quot;<br />&quot;ah, thas wassup. but LOST? is that on tonight?&quot;<br />&quot;yea cuzzo. season finale. last chance for a few weeks to watch Locke make some spiritual musings and whoop on stranded-island-dweller ass.&quot;<br />&quot;sheeit, LOST season finale? thas wassup!&quot;</p><p>will now go like this:</p><p>&quot;hello?&quot;<br />&quot;watt&#39;s good fam. where you at now?&quot;<br />&quot;coolin out with the kasamas at daps&#39; crib. we&#39;re checkin out his comic collection before we watch LOST.&quot;<br />&quot;ah, filipino warrior. but LOST? is that on tonight?&quot;<br />&quot;yea cuzzo. season finale. last chance for a few weeks to watch Locke make some spiritual musings and whoop on stranded-island-dweller ass.&quot;<br />&quot;sheeit, LOST season finale? filipino warrior!&quot;</p><p>happy tuesday stranded-internet-dwellers.</p>-saba<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2006-11-01 | Wednesday</font></strong><br><br>a beautiful, sunny wednesday morning.  big things goin on tonight people. catch your boy Macklemore, one quarter of the elusive group, &quot;Good Medicine,&quot; opening for Devin The Dude tonight at the chop. if you go to the show tonight, clap for them, cheer for them, buy their merch, yell nonsensical things at them... but whatever you do, don&#39;t throw any of them in the briar patch. that&#39;d just be too much. on the other hand, if you&#39;re not feelin the whole hip hop thing, Anthony B, reggae recording artist extraordinaire, will be doin his thing at Neumo&#39;s tonight.  hm, Neumo&#39;s or Chop Suey? this is the the tough question of the year that so many people just have such a hard time answering.  if you don&#39;t catch me at either of the shows above, i&#39;ll be eating naan&amp;paneer and watching LOST at the MassLine office with some of my associates.  hollurr. saba<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2006-10-31 | Tuesday</font></strong><br><br>boo! nah, not &quot;trick-or-treat, smell my feet&quot; boo -- i mean BOO on the governor of oaxaca (pronounced &quot;wa-HA-ka&quot;) for ordering the murder of and sustained violence against underpaid teachers in mexico. the educators took to the streets nearly five months ago calling for better wages; the governor soon demanded that the military remove the group heading-up the protest; the peaceful demonstration recently turned into a mass movement (the &quot;people&#39;s popular assembly&quot;) to oust the governor; yeah, head-crack, head-crack. yesterday around town i saw a few folks &quot;demonstrating,&quot; but aside from that i&#39;m rather surprised at how little reaction there is to such an attrition. teachers are truly the salt of the earth, fam -- if nothing else i ask you keep them in your thoughts and prayers as they offer up the ultimate sacrifice in the path of this cause.<br />                       <br />                         peace to you and yours...<br />                       <br />                         R<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2006-10-27 | Friday</font></strong><br><br>what&#39;sup family?!                          <br />                         <br />                       it&#39;s your cousin <strong>gabe</strong> with an update. a lot of good things soon come, including a more complete website, tourdates down the west coast and back, and some local releases ya&#39;ll are gonna trip off of. for all our <strong>bellingham</strong> folkers, your boy sabzi is gonna be dj&#39;ing at <a href="http://www.nightlightlounge.com/">the nightlight lounge</a> tonight (Fri, 10/27). come throo!  also i&#39;m headed upcoast to <strong>vancouver, b.c.</strong> for a show with <strong>bahamadia</strong>, <a href="http://www.myspace.com/sistahailstorm"><strong>sista hailstorm</strong></a> and <strong>kia kadiri</strong> tonight at <a href="http://www.vecc.bc.ca/">the <strong>vancouver east cultural centre</strong></a>.  there&#39;s more information about <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Military_Commissions_Act">the <strong>military commissions act here</strong></a><strong>...</strong> and ongoing discussions in the <a href="../smf" target="new"><strong>forum</strong></a>.  and don&#39;t forget every saturday on <strong>kbcs 91.3 fm </strong>from<strong> 10 pm - 1 am <a href="http://www.myspace.com/zuluradio">zulu radio</a></strong> is on with your hosts <strong>khazm,</strong> <strong>wd4d</strong> and myself... followed by the illest show regarding hip hop &amp; politics anywhere, <a href="http://www.myspace.com/mrdaveyd"><strong>davey d&#39;s hard knock radio</strong></a>.  (check his <a href="http://www.myspace.com/mrdaveyd">myspace page</a> for the latest episode: slick rick versus homeland security)  gyeah!<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><center><div class="pagenumbers"><A HREF="archive.php?from=275">[&lt;&lt;]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=0">[1]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=5">[2]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=10">[3]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=15">[4]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=20">[5]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=25">[6]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=30">[7]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=35">[8]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=40">[9]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=45">[10]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=50">[11]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=55">[12]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=60">[13]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=65">[14]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=70">[15]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=75">[16]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=80">[17]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=85">[18]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=90">[19]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=95">[20]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=100">[21]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=105">[22]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=110">[23]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=115">[24]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=120">[25]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=125">[26]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=130">[27]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=135">[28]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=140">[29]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=145">[30]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=150">[31]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=155">[32]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=160">[33]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=165">[34]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=170">[35]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=175">[36]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=180">[37]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=185">[38]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=190">[39]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=195">[40]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=200">[41]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=205">[42]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=210">[43]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=215">[44]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=220">[45]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=225">[46]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=230">[47]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=235">[48]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=240">[49]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=245">[50]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=250">[51]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=255">[52]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=260">[53]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=265">[54]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=270">[55]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=275">[56]</A> [57] <A HREF="archive.php?from=285">[58]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=290">[59]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=285">[&gt;&gt;]</